     "result_text_tail": "in the base case. The other three ($7.5M to exit, about 3.4 years to pay back) go to a board vote in 2028, once store-level profit figures are in.\n- I assumed the nine weak stores split their losses and sales evenly, and that the 4-store fee test holds across the chain. Both are noted on their slides.\n\n**Issues to raise before the meeting**\n- **The calendar may not work.** FY2026 is the covenant year, but it probably ends in January 2027, before the February meeting. If so, the first actions can't affect it. Next steps include the CFO opening covenant talks with the lender now.\n- **Two program costs are missing** from the briefing pack: shrink fixes and private-label expansion. They need costing against the $17.5M left under the $25M limit.\n\n**Quality checks**\n- All 163 numbers trace to the briefing pack or a calculation shown in the workbook. There are no \"?\" placeholders.\n- The QA check has no failures. Five warnings remain, all for sidebar dollar figures sized from the pack rather than from the slide's own chart; that is intended.\n- The renderer reports no layout problems.\n- I couldn't preview the slides as images (no converter is installed here, and the sandbox blocks Keynote). Please open the `.pptx` and look through it.\n\nNext I could switch the theme, put all nine store exits into the base case, or add backup slides with the low and high cases in detail.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- harlow-margin-plan.pptx\n- harlow-margin-plan-sources.xlsx\n- harlow-margin-plan.json"
